  "verbalization": "Melitensin is linked to SQ20B through multiple pathways, with the most direct connection emerging from its interaction with NCI-H727, which is a target of (2R)-2-[(2S,5R)-5-ethenyl-5-methyloxolan-2-yl]-6-methylhept-5-en-3-one. This compound, in turn, has SQ20B as its target. However, Melitensin also interacts with CD70 antigen, which is targeted by SB-269970, and SB-269970 itself targets SQ20B. This suggests that Melitensin may act through a common mechanism involving CD70 or other related molecules, which in turn influence SQ20B. The evidence points to a potential role of Melitensin in modulating the activity of CD70 or similar targets, which then lead to SQ20B. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on CD70 or related molecules, which may be critical for the therapeutic effect of Melitensin on SQ20B.",
